{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"5d074d25f423644e0d8f9ba07b77528f04d13d059bc2b7ea5f84ddae36873290","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_5ddbca2ffbf17b89f302d4894c15bd142ef249c184cad8e1398364f8e053ea08","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technically sound extension of Generative Adversarial Imitation Learning to the third-person setting by incorporating domain confusion. The methodological formulation is clear, and the experimental design effectively validates the core claims through ablation studies and sensitivity analyses on standard MuJoCo environments. While the scope is limited to simple tasks, the work is complete and provides sufficient detail for reproducibility.","paper_id":"B16dGcqlx","paper_identity_sha256":"9f79d5d228096ff7758af3cc8ad06d2a675653de0236f314527c8b236fdee854","prompt_identity_sha256":"b1f7b20dda9df1f0a9cc80bce1539fc695d65466e5b704c3e1f989df815ca56b","raw_response_sha256":"ef22c38acb01992b136d660c93cc32a4361032d355af560cf1621d595e2ba864","request_identity_sha256":"cd2d65b88cff12eaad3145dcc0990acb0ff9a2c34dfc7a3b2349497685ea3f78","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"6b42c038036b3e7698bdf7544dfc6c49b61bab92c4126345f4762d53cb12259d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-021","SRC-022"],"review_text":"The proposed method is technically sound and well-formulated. The authors correctly identify that standard imitation learning discriminators fail in third-person settings because they learn domain-specific features rather than task-relevant ones. The solution, which partitions the discriminator into a feature extractor and a classifier and applies a gradient reversal layer to the feature extractor, is a mathematically consistent application of domain confusion techniques. The objective function is clearly defined, and the use of the gradient flipping technique to enforce domain invariance is appropriate for the stated goal of recovering a domain-agnostic representation.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-MET"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-031","SRC-032"],"review_text":"The experimental design is adequate for the scope of the paper, which focuses on simple environments. The authors utilize three standard MuJoCo tasks (Point, Reacher, Inverted Pendulum) with distinct visual differences between expert and novice domains. The evaluation includes ablation studies that isolate the contributions of domain confusion and multi-time-step inputs, demonstrating that domain confusion is essential for performance. Additionally, sensitivity analyses for the domain confusion weight and look-ahead frames provide insight into the algorithm's robustness. The experiments convincingly validate the claim that the method can learn from third-person demonstrations in these simple settings.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-024","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The paper provides sufficient detail for reproducibility. Algorithm 1 clearly outlines the training procedure, including the initialization of the memory bank, the sampling of expert and novice rollouts, and the alternating optimization steps. The authors specify the use of the ADAM optimizer for the discriminator components and TRPO for the policy. Hyperparameters such as the domain confusion weight and the number of look-ahead frames are discussed, and the specific values used in the main experiments are indicated. The description of the environments and the visual modifications applied to create the third-person setting is clear, allowing for the replication of the experimental setup.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-REP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-008","SRC-009","SRC-010","SRC-011"],"review_text":"The paper positions itself well within the context of prior work. It distinguishes its contribution from standard behavioral cloning and inverse reinforcement learning by highlighting the lack of observation correspondence in third-person settings. The authors appropriately cite and build upon recent work in Generative Adversarial Imitation Learning (Ho & Ermon, 2016) and domain confusion (Tzeng et al., 2014). The related work section effectively explains why existing methods are not directly applicable and how the proposed approach addresses the specific challenges of third-person imitation from raw sensory data.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-CMP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-033"],"review_text":"The statistical rigor is appropriate for the experimental scale. The authors report learning curves averaged over 5 trials with error bars representing one standard deviation, which provides a reasonable indication of the variance in the training process. The ablation studies and sensitivity analyses are presented with sufficient detail to assess the stability of the results. While the number of trials is modest, it is consistent with the computational cost of the RL training procedure and the simple nature of the tasks. The reported improvements are supported by the visual evidence in the figures, and the authors are transparent about the initial instability of the training process.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-STA"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"427905d1e9fd3b5b399ce74e0008ff0ae79b7696018213cc2684ce9a4a6f13ad","paper_id":"B16dGcqlx","paper_ordinal":3,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"ef22c38acb01992b136d660c93cc32a4361032d355af560cf1621d595e2ba864","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B16dGcqlx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"03a583b87993b977ebf29464cb3417e9815c4ea29787acb754c01506a780a915","request_identity_sha256":"cd2d65b88cff12eaad3145dcc0990acb0ff9a2c34dfc7a3b2349497685ea3f78","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":1066,"prompt_tokens":18758,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19824},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"cd2d65b88cff12eaad3145dcc0990acb0ff9a2c34dfc7a3b2349497685ea3f78","role":"QUAL","role_ordinal":0,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}